# API & Infra Conventions

## Auth

- Public: `/authentication/register`, `/login`, `/refresh-token`
- Protected: middleware `Auth(jwtSecret)`
- Access vs refresh dibedakan lewat claim `type`
- Token expired message: `"Unauthorized: Token expired"` (selaras Wisteria interceptor)

## Headers

- `apikey: <API_KEY>` wajib di `/api/v1`
- `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` untuk route protected

## Redis

- Cache read-through di service layer
- Invalidate list/detail pada create/update/delete
- Key pattern: `product:{id}`, `products:user:{userId}` / cursor list cache

## Kafka

- Publish dari service setelah persist sukses (`product.created` / updated / deleted)
- Topics: `products.events` + DLQ `products.events.dlq`
- Worker (`cmd/worker`, group `golang-be-worker`) → Mongo audit; exhausted → DLQ
- Notifier (di API process, group `golang-be-notifier`) → WebSocket fan-out
- Offset commit hanya setelah side effect sukses (at-least-once)
- Publish event async via `go` + `context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), ...)`
  (jangan reuse request context — bisa cancel saat handler return)

## Goroutine (contoh di project)

- `cmd/api`: listen di goroutine + graceful shutdown via fx lifecycle
- `product` service: publish Kafka / index Typesense di background supaya HTTP tidak menunggu

## REST resources

- Plural nouns: `/products`
- Method: GET list/detail, POST create, PUT update, DELETE delete
- Ownership check di service (`userId` match) → `ErrForbidden`; role `admin` boleh delete any
